.TH DUK 1 "November 2025" "duk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
duk \- CLI tool for downloading financial market data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B duk
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG_PATH\fR]
.I subcommand
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B duk
is a command-line tool and library for downloading financial market data and
performing data preprocessing. It provides access to various financial APIs
and supports data transformation and analysis.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show program's version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICONFIG_PATH\fR ", " \-\-config " " \fICONFIG_PATH\fR
Path to configuration file (default: ~/.dukrc).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B ph
Download security price history from Financial Modeling Prep API.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B duk
reads configuration from
.I ~/.dukrc
by default. The configuration file uses TOML format.
.PP
Example configuration:
.PP
.nf
.RS
[api]
fmp_api_key = "YOUR_API_KEY"

[output]
output_dir = "./var"

[logging]
log_dir = "./var/logs"
log_level = "INFO"
log_to_file = true
log_to_stdout = true
.RE
.fi
.PP
To get an API key, visit:
.I https://financialmodelingprep.com/developer/docs/
.SH SUBCOMMAND: ph
Download security price history from Financial Modeling Prep API.
.SS Synopsis
.B duk ph
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR \fILIMIT\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIFROM_DATE\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fITO_DATE\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR]
[\fB\-\-fields\fR \fIFIELDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
.I symbol
.SS Description
Downloads historical price data for a given security symbol. The symbol is
case-insensitive and will be converted to uppercase for the API call.
.SS Options
.TP
.I symbol
Security symbol (e.g., IBM, AAPL). Required positional argument.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-l " " \fILIMIT\fR ", " \-\-limit " " \fILIMIT\fR
Number of most recent data points to return (default: 5).
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFROM_DATE\fR ", " \-\-from\-date " " \fIFROM_DATE\fR
Start date in YYYY-MM-DD format.
.TP
.BR \-t " " \fITO_DATE\fR ", " \-\-to\-date " " \fITO_DATE\fR
End date in YYYY-MM-DD format.
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIOUTPUT\fR ", " \-\-output " " \fIOUTPUT\fR
Output file path (default: stdout).
.TP
.BR \-\-fields " " \fIFIELDS\fR
Comma-separated list of fields to display (default: date,close,volume).
Available fields include: date, open, high, low, close, volume, and others
depending on the data source.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: csv, json, or table (default: table).
.SS Examples
.PP
Get 5 most recent data points for IBM:
.RS
.B duk ph IBM
.RE
.PP
Get 10 most recent data points for Apple:
.RS
.B duk ph AAPL \-l 10
.RE
.PP
Get data for a specific date range:
.RS
.B duk ph MSFT \-f 2023-01-01 \-t 2023-12-31
.RE
.PP
Save output to CSV file:
.RS
.B duk ph IBM \-o ibm_history.csv \-\-format csv
.RE
.PP
Display specific fields:
.RS
.B duk ph IBM \-\-fields date,close,open,high,low,volume
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dukrc
User configuration file (TOML format).
.TP
.I ./var/logs/duk.log
Default log file location.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
No environment variables are currently used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error (e.g., API error, configuration error, invalid input)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Download 5 most recent price points for IBM:
.RS
.B duk ph IBM
.RE
.PP
Download price history for a date range and save as JSON:
.RS
.B duk ph AAPL \-f 2024-01-01 \-t 2024-12-31 \-o apple.json \-\-format json
.RE
